  "title": "dumpcap: stop sending EOF to tshark when using ring-buffer",
  "description": "In a previous commit ([11a9a501fb004bd3259f457714670ffb6d3d21e9](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/11a9a501fb004bd3259f457714670ffb6d3d21e9)),\nthe code that handles ring-buffer file changes was moved to a\nfunction called capture_loop_wrote_one_packet. This function is\ncalled by the appropriate pcap_handler function. Originally this\nwas handled in the capture loop, capture_loop_start. For some\nreason, moving this into the pcap handler has caused dumpcap to\nsend an EOF to tshark, causing tshark to stop when writing to\nSTDOUT. Moving this code back into the loop seems to fix the\nissue. I haven't been able to thoroughly step through the code\nto see why dumpcap sends the EOF.",
