      "title": "dumpcap: stop sending EOF to tshark when using ring-buffer",
      "message": "dumpcap: stop sending EOF to tshark when using ring-buffer\n\nIn a previous commit a while back, the code that handles ring-buffer\nfile changes was moved to a function called\ncapture_loop_wrote_one_packet. This function is called by the\nappropriate pcap_handler function. Originally this was handled\nin the capture loop, capture_loop_start. For some reason, moving\nthis into the pcap handler has caused dumpcap to send an EOF\nto tshark, causing tshark to stop when writing to STDOUT. Moving\nthis code back into the loop seems to fix the issue. I haven't\nbeen able to thoroughly step through the code to see why dumpcap\nsends the EOF.\n",
      "author_name": "Bob Wintemberg",
      "author_email": "bob@wint.email",
